From d55a4f6f849b3716c7725a7ba6f53dab3baa34aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:01:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [e-acsl] mark formal parameters as initialized on
 function entry

On function entry, E-ACSL registered each tracked formal with
__e_acsl_store_block but never marked it initialized, although the
caller has just written it. Any check that reads the shadow memory of a
formal then failed on every call, whatever the caller passed:
- \initialized(&s.f) on a field of a struct passed by value, in a user
  annotation (issue #177) or in an RTE guard with -e-acsl-rte-initialized;
- \initialized(p) on a pointer to a scalar formal, even after an
  explicit assignment, since add_initializer emits no full_init for an
  assignment to a whole formal.

The rest of E-ACSL already assumes formals are initialized
(add_initializer and needs_guard skip them), and globals are stored and
marked initialized the same way (global_observer.ml). Emit
__e_acsl_full_init right after the __e_acsl_store_block of each formal.

Most E-ACSL oracles (gen_*.c) change: each gets one
__e_acsl_full_init((void *)(& p)); line after the store_block of a
formal. Add bts/issue-framac-177.c as a regression test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
